# Local secrets for `wrangler dev` (copy to .dev.vars; never committed). Production: `npx wrangler secret put <NAME>`.
# Development values only, never a production one (a separate development OAuth client, a throwaway key).
# Signs sessions, match tickets and the Worker <-> Durable Object internal header: a long random string.
JWT_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
# Required outside local dev (POST /api/guest answers 503 'turnstile_unconfigured' without it on a deploy).
# TURNSTILE_SECRET=
# Comma-separated browser origins allowed for CORS and WebSocket upgrades (unset = '*' / any Origin, dev only).
# VITE_ORIGINS=https://your-game.example
# Local OAuth testing only: the origin the provider redirects back to (the Vite page, which proxies
# /api to this Worker), e.g. http://localhost:5173. Production uses the request's own origin.
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
# Community nodes (nodes/), optional: without the control key (and the NODES binding with its R2
# buckets) the Worker never sends a match to a node. Production's private half is
# nodes/.keys/control.json's (`npm run keys` in nodes/); its public half is the
# NODE_CONTROL_PUBLIC_KEY var. For development make a new pair instead, never from nodes/.keys/
# (the real key may be there): README, "Community nodes", has the one line that writes both halves
# here without printing them (a .dev.vars value overrides the committed var).
# Production sets NODE_CONTROL_PRIVATE_KEY and NODE_TRUSTED_OPERATORS with `npx wrangler versions
# secret put <NAME>`, never with `wrangler secret put`: that one deploys at once, and a deploy
# resets the running matches (README, "Community nodes"). The next deploy ships them.
# NODE_CONTROL_PRIVATE_KEY=
# NODE_CONTROL_PUBLIC_KEY=
# The project's account ids (16 hex characters each), comma-separated: their nodes are trusted.
# Locally: the id of the account ENTRAR (DEV) made (DEV_AUTH below), then restart and sign in again;
# PERFIL › CUENTA DEL PROYECTO then shows CONTROL DE NODOS. A dev sign-in lasts 15 minutes at level 2.
# NODE_TRUSTED_OPERATORS=
# Locally only: the Worker's own origin (your port), so the install lines and tickets name it, and
# a loopback base lets the object probe the nodes on this machine. It overrides the committed var.
# NODES_PUBLIC_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8787
# Your own copy only, commented here (server/test/dev-signin.test.mjs): the dev sign-in.
# DEV_AUTH=1
# A staff-only Discord channel's webhook URL: the node control plane posts its ALERT lines there
# (production: `npx wrangler versions secret put NODE_ALERT_WEBHOOK` too).
# NODE_ALERT_WEBHOOK=
